meta {
  name: Create Celcom Sender
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/admin/celcom-senders
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  X-Admin-Secret: {{admin_secret}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "shortcode": "LigiOpen",
    "apiKey": "<Celcom-issued API key for this shortcode>"
  }
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
  timeout: 0
}

docs {
  ## Create Celcom Sender

  Bruno: `admin/Create Celcom Sender`

  Registers a Celcom shortcode (e.g. `LigiOpen`, `KaaKazini`) with its own API key. Every SMS
  send request's `sender` field (see `sms/Send SMS`) must match a shortcode registered here -
  `sms/send` looks up credentials by that exact value and fails with a clear error if none are
  active for it.

  - `partnerId` is optional and defaults to `"954"` (every shortcode registered so far shares
    this Celcom partner ID) - only pass it if Celcom assigns a different one to a new shortcode.
  - `shortcode` must be unique; creating a duplicate is rejected.
  - `apiKey` is stored in plaintext (unlike `api-clients`' `apiSecret`, this is a credential we
    use to call Celcom, not one used to authenticate callers to us, so it can't be hashed) and is
    returned as-is on every read here - this endpoint is already gated by `X-Admin-Secret`.

  Code source: `CelcomSenderControllerImpl.createCelcomSender` / `CelcomSenderServiceImpl.createCelcomSender`.
}
